ta</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Romero</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Outbreak of extended-spectrum beta-lactamase producing Serratia marcescens in an intensive care unit</article-title><source>FEMS Immunol Med Microbiol</source><year>1994</year><volume>10</volume><fpage>39</fpage><lpage>46</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7874077</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B7"><label>7</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Schaberg</surname><given-names>DR</given-names></name><name><surname>Alford</surname><given-names>RH</given-names></name><name><surname>Anderson</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Farmer</surname><given-names>JJ</given-names><suffix>III</suffix></name><name><surname>Melly</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><name><surname>Schaffner</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>An outbreak of nosocomial infection due to multiply resistant Serratia marcescens: evidence of interhospital spread</article-title><source>J Infect Dis</source><year>1976</year><volume>134</volume><fpage>181</fpage><lpage>188</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">787446</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B8"><label>8</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bagattini</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Crispino</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Gentile</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Barretta</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Schiavone</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Boccia</surname><given-names>MC</given-names></name><name><surname>Triassi</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Zarrilli</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A